Task: Establish the accessibility baseline (Red phase)
Phase: 0 (Harvest & Baseline)
Scope: packages/{react,vue,svelte}/tests/a11yBaseline.test.*

Baseline on untouched base: 279 passed, 0 failed.
After adding baseline specs: 5 failed, 3 passed (8 new).

Documented failures, all genuine defects on main:
  1. React  slider has no tabindex - unreachable by keyboard
  2. React  ArrowRight does not advance progress
  3. Vue    ArrowRight does not advance progress
  4. Vue    aria-disabled absent (React and Svelte both ship it)
  5. Svelte ArrowRight does not advance progress

Finding: role=slider placement diverges across adapters. React puts it
on the container div; Vue and Svelte put it on an SVG <g> handle with
tabindex=0. Specs were rewritten mid-task to locate the widget by
[role=slider] rather than a hardcoded container, so they remain valid
under either normalisation.

Open decision blocking Phase 3: where role=slider belongs. Keyboard
handlers and tabindex must sit on that element. Note that tabindex on
an SVG <g> is not reliably focusable across browsers - WebKit in
particular - which the Playwright matrix in Phase 5 would surface.

Spec deltas for the three adapters currently say 'the container MUST
expose tabindex'. That wording is correct only for React and needs
correcting once placement is decided.
